 A and B, the angular acceleration of the pulley, the tension in each side of the cable, the kinetic friction force, the final velocity of the blocks, the work done by the applied force, the work done by friction, the change in kinetic energy of the system, and the final rotational kinetic energy of the pulley. Show the governing equations and verify the results using Newton's second law, the rotational equation of motion, the no-slip constraint, and the work-energy principle."}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['work', 'time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'description': 'Calculate normal stress.\n\n